    "lawCode": "Amd §9-209, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3045A\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the election law, in relation to\ncanvass of ballots\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides that the Board Of Elections shall cast and canvas any\nballot in which a voter was entitled to vote, so long as such voter\n\"substantially complied\" with the requirements of filling out an absen-\ntee, military, special ballots and ballots cast by voters with registra-\ntion poll records missing, i.e., affidavit ballots.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAdds authorization to the Board Of Elections that empowers them to cast\nand canvas any ballot in which a voter was entitled to vote, so long as\nsuch voter \"substantially complied\" with the requirements of filling out\nan absentee, military, special ballot and/or a ballot cast by a voter\nwith registration poll records missing, i.e., affidavit ballots.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill ensures that the votes of individuals who are entitled to vote\nat elections will be cast so long as there is substantial compliance\nwith the requirements to obtain such a ballot, like the filling out of\npaperwork, or the cataloguing of past addresses.\n\nThis bill is necessary because the current law is of exploited by those\nseeking to invalidate ballots by employing hyper-technical legal chal-\nlenges to ballots in an all-too-often successful effort to deny a person\ntheir constitutional right to vote.\n\nThis language will allow the validity of the ballot to be determined\nbased upon compliance with the language of the statute and the actions\nand intentions of the voter, without limiting the state's ability to\nprotect against voter fraud.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSimilar Bill: S 1265 COMRIE Same as A 7484 Cahill (MS).\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
